<meta type=article>
  <title | Config edge-case fixture>
  <author | Test Author>
</meta>

<config ref-prefix-eqn="Eq.">

<section | Trailing whitespace after a sigil close>

A sigil heading with trailing whitespace after the `#>` (formerly PG-11)
must still be recognized as a flow construct. Before the fix it was
silently reclaimed as inline text. The line below has a space after the
closer; the sigil heading must produce a `<sub-section>`.

<## A sigil with trailing whitespace ##>

Surrounding prose continues to render normally below the sigil heading.

<section | Cross-reference using the ref-prefix override>

The `<config ref-prefix-eqn="Eq.">` at the document top must produce
"Eq. 1" when this section references an equation. The config kwarg is on a
top-level `<config>` (existing path), proving the existing single-top-level
discovery still works alongside the new recursive walk.

<$$ #eqn:newton | F = ma $$>

Newton's second law is shown in <ref @eqn:newton> — this should render as
"Eq. 1" (not "equation 1") because of the ref-prefix override above.

<section | Nested config block is now read>

A nested `<config>` block (formerly PG-9, "deeply-nested `<config>` not
read") is now discovered by the recursive walk. The block below sits
inside this section, not at root; before the fix its `ref-prefix-fig`
override would be silently ignored. With the fix, a figure ref following
it should render with "Fig." instead of "figure".

<config ref-prefix-fig="Fig.">
